NEW SHINOBI ONBOARDING -- DESERT SURVIVAL BRIEFING

Welcome, recruit. Before you carry the Sand headband beyond these walls, learn
the first truth of Sunagakure: the desert is neither friend nor enemy. It is
indifferent, and it kills the careless.

Remember these rules:
- Water is life and water is rationed. Never drink beyond your allotment; never
  waste a drop. Wasting water endangers your whole squad.
- Move at dawn and dusk. The midday sun will fell you; the night will freeze you.
- In a sandstorm, do not fight the wind. Anchor low, cover eyes and mouth, and
  wait. Only qualified wind-users disperse storms, and never the great ones.
- Trust your training, not the dunes. Sand shifts and erases every trail.
- Watch for scorpions and vipers; report bites to the medical corps at once.

Master the desert and you need fear few enemies within it. This briefing pairs
with your mandatory survival syllabus. Ask your instructor for anything unclear.
